  "description": "RAGSOL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H118 Mn7 N6 Nd3 O41,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.973-3.992 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 82.92-128.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H127Mn7N9Nd3O41. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
